🚀 Logs Deep Dive

🔹 What are Logs? 📜
 Logs are records of events generated by systems and applications.
 They capture what happened inside your system at a specific time.
 👉 “What exactly happened?”

🔹 Why it matters in real-world? 🏗️
 When something breaks in production, metrics show the problem…
 👉 Logs show the exact reason behind it 🔍
They are your first tool for debugging issues.

🔹 Log Levels: ⚡
✔ INFO ℹ️
Normal system activity
Example: Service started successfully
✔ DEBUG 🐞
Detailed internal information
Used during development/troubleshooting
✔ ERROR ❌
Something failed
Requires immediate attention

🔹 Structured vs Unstructured Logs: 📊
✔ Structured Logs 📁
Format: JSON or key-value
Easy to search and analyze
👉 Example:
 {"status":500, "msg":"Server error"}
✔ Unstructured Logs 📄
Plain text format
Harder to analyze
👉 Example:
 Server failed with error code 500

🔹 Real-world Example: 💡
Your application crashes 🚨
👉 Metrics show: High error rate
 👉 Logs show:
ERROR → Database connection failed
DEBUG → Connection timeout issue
✅ Logs help you pinpoint the exact problem

🔹 Key Concepts to Remember: 🧠
✔ Logs = Event records 📜
 ✔ INFO = Normal activity ℹ️
 ✔ DEBUG = Detailed info 🐞
 ✔ ERROR = Failure ❌
 ✔ Structured logs = Easy analysis 📊
